      "entryId": "exo-20-8",
      "field": "principle",
      "after": "The Fourth Commandment: Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy. Grounded explicitly in the Creation Sabbath of Genesis 2:2-3 and sealed as a perpetual covenant sign in Exodus 31:16-17, the Sabbath is proclaimed as a holy delight by Isaiah (Isa 58:13-14). Jesus declares Himself Lord of the Sabbath (Mark 2:27-28) customarily observes it (Luke 4:16) and Hebrews affirms a Sabbath-rest at the end of the story (sabbatismos) remaining for the people of God (Heb 4:9). First principle: the Sabbath is a moral, perpetual creation ordinance memorializing the Creator's rest and pointing forward to the finished rest of redemption.",
